# Implementation Plan - Custom Climate Chart Visualizations

The goal of this task is to enhance the climate dashboard by replacing solid/standard color lines with a dynamic dot-based (or dashed) visualization indicating temperature trends (rising, stable, declining). We will also unify the colors across all three sections to use exactly 2–3 colors (Red for rising, Amber for stable, Blue for declining), style the anomaly bar chart consistently, and upgrade the sidebar legend/key with precise visual symbols.

## Data Accuracy Guarantees

> [!IMPORTANT]
> To ensure 100% data plotting accuracy and maintain the precise variation and trends of the max, min, peak, and summer temperatures:
> 1. We will **retain the exact same `dataKey` mappings** (`peakMaxTemp`, `summerMaxTemp`, `maxTemp`, `minTemp`, `forecastPeak`, `forecastMax`, `forecastSummer`, `forecastMin`) on all `Line` components.
> 2. The `type="monotone"` property is preserved for smooth cubic interpolation, which guarantees the lines track the exact data variations.
> 3. The `CustomTempDot` component will read the values directly from Recharts' internal dataset props (`seriesData[index]`) using the corresponding `dataKey`, ensuring the dots are placed at the exact mathematical coordinates on the canvas.

## Proposed Changes

We will modify [app/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Midtown Computers/OneDrive/Desktop/climate reserach/climate_research_project/app/page.tsx) to implement:
1. A new `CustomTempDot` component that dynamically colors dots based on whether the temperature rose, declined, or remained stable compared to the previous year.
2. A streamlined, less colorful styling for all charts (Historical Trends and ML Forecast lines will use thin, neutral slate strokes, leaving the color entirely to the dynamic trend dots).
3. The anomaly bar chart styled consistently using the same Red (positive anomaly), Amber (neutral anomaly), and Blue (negative anomaly) color palette.
4. A highly detailed and premium sidebar key replacing the simple text list with actual visual representations (SVG line strokes, dots, and bar indicators).

